---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy - Banners All Over" description="Privacy Policy for Banners All Over Shopify app - How we collect, use, and protect your data">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center text-bao-blue hover:text-bao-blue-600 transition-colors mb-6">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Home
      </a>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600">Last Updated: December 2, 2025</p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mt-2">Effective Date: December 2, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">1. Introduction</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Welcome to Banners All Over ("we," "us," "our," or "BAO"). We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring the security of your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our Shopify application and related services (collectively, the "Service").
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          This Privacy Policy applies to information we collect:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Through the Banners All Over Shopify app</li>
          <li>Via our website at [website URL]</li>
          <li>Through email, support tickets, and other communications with us</li>
          <li>From your Shopify store when you install our app</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Please read this Privacy Policy carefully. By using our Service, you consent to the practices described in this policy. If you do not agree with our policies and practices, do not install or use the Service.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-bao-blue p-4 rounded mb-4">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
            <strong>Data Controller:</strong> Banners All Over is the data controller responsible for your personal information. Our contact details are provided in Section 14 of this policy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Information We Collect -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Account and Installation Information</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When you install Banners All Over through the Shopify App Store, we collect:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Store Information:</strong> Your Shopify store name, store URL, and store ID</li>
          <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Store owner's email address and name</li>
          <li><strong>Subscription Details:</strong> Your selected pricing tier and billing information (processed by Shopify)</li>
          <li><strong>Installation Date:</strong> When you installed or last updated the app</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Content You Create</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When you use Banners All Over to create banners, we collect and store:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Banner Configurations:</strong> Text, images, videos, links, and design settings for your banners</li>
          <li><strong>Media Files:</strong> Images and videos you upload for use in banners</li>
          <li><strong>Display Settings:</strong> Placement rules, scheduling, targeting conditions, and animation preferences</li>
          <li><strong>Product Information:</strong> Product IDs and data when using Product banner types</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Communications</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When you contact us for support or feedback, we collect:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Contact Form Data:</strong> Email address, subject line, message content, and timestamp</li>
          <li><strong>Support Correspondence:</strong> Email communications and support ticket information</li>
          <li><strong>Feedback and Survey Responses:</strong> When you choose to provide feedback</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.2 Information We Collect Automatically</h3>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Usage and Technical Data</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When you use our Service, we automatically collect certain technical information:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>App Usage Data:</strong> Number of banners created, features used, settings configured, and interaction patterns</li>
          <li><strong>Device Information:</strong> Browser type and version, operating system, device type (desktop/tablet/mobile)</li>
          <li><strong>Log Data:</strong> IP address, access times, pages viewed, time spent on pages, referring URLs</li>
          <li><strong>Error Logs:</strong> Technical errors, crash reports, and diagnostic information</li>
          <li><strong>Performance Metrics:</strong> Load times, response times, and app performance data</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Shopify Store Data</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          With your authorization through Shopify's OAuth process, we access:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Product Catalog:</strong> Product names, descriptions, images, and IDs (for Product banner functionality)</li>
          <li><strong>Theme Information:</strong> To ensure banner compatibility and styling</li>
          <li><strong>Store Settings:</strong> Currency, timezone, and locale information</li>
          <li><strong>Collection Data:</strong> For display rules and targeting features</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Note:</strong> We do NOT access or collect your customers' personal information, payment information, order details, or customer purchase history unless explicitly required for specific features and disclosed separately.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.3 Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h3>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Current Status</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>We currently do NOT use cookies or tracking technologies on our marketing website.</strong> Our website is cookie-free.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Future Implementation</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          In the future, we may implement the following types of cookies and tracking:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Strictly Necessary Cookies:</strong> Essential for app functionality and security (no consent required)</li>
          <li><strong>Functional Cookies:</strong> To remember your preferences and settings</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics Cookies:</strong> Google Analytics or similar to understand how users interact with our Service</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing Cookies:</strong> For advertising and marketing purposes</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If we implement cookies in the future, we will:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Provide a cookie consent banner before setting non-essential cookies</li>
          <li>Allow you to manage your cookie preferences</li>
          <li>Update this Privacy Policy with detailed cookie information</li>
          <li>Publish a separate <a href="/legal/cookies" class="text-bao-blue hover:underline">Cookie Policy</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">2.4 Information We Do NOT Collect</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          For transparency, we explicitly do NOT collect:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Your customers' personal information (names, addresses, emails)</li>
          <li>Payment or credit card information (handled entirely by Shopify)</li>
          <li>Order details or purchase history</li>
          <li>Social Security numbers or government identification</li>
          <li>Financial account information</li>
          <li>Health or medical information</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- How We Use Information -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We use the information we collect for the following purposes:
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.1 Service Delivery and Operation</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Provide, operate, and maintain the Banners All Over service</li>
          <li>Display banners on your Shopify store according to your configurations</li>
          <li>Store and process your banner content and settings</li>
          <li>Authenticate your access to the app</li>
          <li>Enforce subscription tier limitations (number of banners, slides, features)</li>
          <li>Process product data for Product banner functionality</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.2 Service Improvement and Development</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Analyze usage patterns to improve features and user experience</li>
          <li>Identify and fix bugs, errors, and technical issues</li>
          <li>Develop new features and functionality (including future AI features)</li>
          <li>Test and optimize app performance</li>
          <li>Conduct research and analytics using aggregated, anonymized data</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.3 Customer Support and Communication</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Respond to your support requests and inquiries</li>
          <li>Send transactional emails (subscription confirmations, renewal notices, etc.)</li>
          <li>Provide technical assistance and troubleshooting</li>
          <li>Send important service announcements and updates</li>
          <li>Notify you of changes to our Terms or Privacy Policy</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.4 Security and Fraud Prevention</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Detect and prevent fraudulent, abusive, or illegal activities</li>
          <li>Monitor and analyze security threats</li>
          <li>Verify identity and authenticate users</li>
          <li>Protect our systems and infrastructure</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.5 Legal Compliance</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Comply with legal obligations and regulatory requirements</li>
          <li>Respond to legal requests, court orders, or government demands</li>
          <li>Enforce our Terms of Service</li>
          <li>Protect our rights, property, and safety, and that of our users</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">3.6 Marketing (With Consent)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          With your explicit opt-in consent, we may:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Send newsletters and product updates</li>
          <li>Inform you about new features and promotions</li>
          <li>Conduct surveys and request feedback</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          You can opt-out of marketing communications at any time by clicking the "unsubscribe" link in emails or contacting us directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Legal Basis (GDPR) -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">4. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          For users in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom, and Switzerland, we process your personal data based on the following legal grounds:
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.1 Contractual Necessity</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Processing is necessary to perform our contract with you (Terms of Service):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Providing the banner creation and display service</li>
          <li>Managing your account and subscription</li>
          <li>Processing billing through Shopify</li>
          <li>Delivering customer support</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.2 Legitimate Interests</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Processing is necessary for our legitimate business interests (which are not overridden by your rights):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Improving and optimizing our Service</li>
          <li>Detecting and preventing fraud and security threats</li>
          <li>Conducting analytics using aggregated, anonymized data</li>
          <li>Developing new features and products</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.3 Legal Obligation</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Processing is necessary to comply with legal obligations:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Tax and accounting requirements</li>
          <li>Responding to lawful requests from authorities</li>
          <li>Compliance with data protection laws</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">4.4 Consent</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Processing based on your explicit consent:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Marketing communications and newsletters</li>
          <li>Non-essential cookies (if implemented)</li>
          <li>Participation in surveys or beta programs</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          You may withdraw your consent at any time by contacting us or using the opt-out mechanisms provided.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Data Sharing -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">5. How We Share Your Information</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We do NOT sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties. We may share your information only in the following circumstances:
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">5.1 Service Providers and Partners</h3>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Current Third Parties:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Shopify:</strong> For app hosting, billing, authentication, and store data access
            <br><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">Privacy Policy: <a href="https://www.shopify.com/legal/privacy" class="text-bao-blue hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.shopify.com/legal/privacy</a></span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Future Third Parties (to be implemented):</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          When we implement additional features, we may share data with:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Cloud Hosting Providers:</strong> [AWS/Google Cloud/etc.] for data storage and processing</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics Services:</strong> Google Analytics for usage analytics (anonymized data only)</li>
          <li><strong>Email Service Providers:</strong> [To be determined] for transactional and marketing emails</li>
          <li><strong>AI Service Providers:</strong> OpenAI, Anthropic, or similar for AI features (if implemented)</li>
          <li><strong>CDN Providers:</strong> For content delivery and media hosting</li>
          <li><strong>Customer Support Tools:</strong> For ticket management and support communications</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          All third-party service providers are carefully selected and required to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Process data only as instructed by us</li>
          <li>Implement appropriate security measures</li>
          <li>Comply with applicable data protection laws</li>
          <li>Use data only for the specific services they provide to us</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">5.2 Business Transfers</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If we are involved in a merger, acquisition, asset sale, or bankruptcy, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction. We will notify you of any such change and any choices you may have.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">5.3 Legal Requirements</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We may disclose your information if required to do so by law or in response to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Legal process, court orders, or government requests</li>
          <li>Requests from law enforcement or regulatory authorities</li>
          <li>National security or law enforcement requirements</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">5.4 Protection of Rights</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We may disclose information when we believe it is necessary to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>Enforce our Terms of Service</li>
          <li>Protect our rights, property, or safety</li>
          <li>Protect the rights, property, or safety of our users or the public</li>
          <li>Detect, prevent, or address fraud, security, or technical issues</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">5.5 Aggregated and Anonymized Data</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          We may share aggregated, anonymized data that cannot identify you personally for research, marketing, analytics, or other business purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- International Data Transfers -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">6. International Data Transfers</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Your information may be transferred to, stored, and processed in countries other than your country of residence, including [SPECIFY COUNTRIES/REGIONS WHERE DATA IS STORED].
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          These countries may have data protection laws that are different from the laws of your country. However, we take steps to ensure that your information receives an adequate level of protection wherever it is processed.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">6.1 Safeguards for EU Data Transfers</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          For transfers of personal data from the EEA, UK, or Switzerland to countries that do not provide an adequate level of data protection, we implement appropriate safeguards, including:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs):</strong> Approved by the European Commission</li>
          <li><strong>Adequacy Decisions:</strong> Relying on European Commission adequacy decisions where applicable</li>
          <li><strong>Binding Corporate Rules:</strong> For transfers within corporate groups (if applicable)</li>
          <li><strong>Additional Technical Measures:</strong> Encryption, pseudonymization, and access controls</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-700">
          You may request a copy of the safeguards we have in place by contacting us at the details provided in Section 14.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Data Retention -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">7. Data Retention</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We retain your personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this Privacy Policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">7.1 Retention Periods</h3>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-300">
                <th class="text-left py-2 font-semibold text-gray-700">Data Type</th>
                <th class="text-left py-2 font-semibold text-gray-700">Retention Period</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-gray-700">
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Active Account Data</td>
                <td class="py-2">Duration of subscription + 30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Deleted Account Data</td>
                <td class="py-2">30 days from deletion (then permanent removal)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Banner Content & Media</td>
                <td class="py-2">Duration of subscription + 30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Contact Form Submissions</td>
                <td class="py-2">2 years from submission</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Support Correspondence</td>
                <td class="py-2">3 years from last interaction</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Technical Logs</td>
                <td class="py-2">90 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2">Billing Records</td>
                <td class="py-2">7 years (tax/legal requirements)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2">Aggregated Analytics</td>
                <td class="py-2">Indefinitely (anonymized, non-personal)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">7.2 Retention Criteria</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We determine retention periods based on:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li>The length of time we have an ongoing relationship with you</li>
          <li>Whether we have a legal obligation to retain the data</li>
          <li>Whether retention is necessary for our legitimate business interests</li>
          <li>Whether retention is advisable in light of our legal position (statute of limitations, litigation, regulatory investigation)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">7.3 Deletion Process</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          When data is no longer needed, we securely delete or anonymize it using industry-standard methods. Data in backups is deleted according to our backup retention schedule (typically within 90 days of primary deletion).
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Data Security -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">8. Data Security</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          We implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures to protect your personal information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">8.1 Technical Safeguards</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Encryption:</strong> Data in transit is encrypted using TLS/HTTPS protocols; sensitive data at rest is encrypted</li>
          <li><strong>Access Controls:</strong> Role-based access control (RBAC) limits who can access personal data</li>
          <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Secure authentication through Shopify OAuth</li>
          <li><strong>Network Security:</strong> Firewalls, intrusion detection, and network monitoring</li>
          <li><strong>Secure Development:</strong> Security testing, code reviews, and vulnerability scanning</li>
          <li><strong>Regular Updates:</strong> Security patches and updates applied promptly</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">8.2 Organizational Safeguards</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-4 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Employee Training:</strong> Regular security and privacy training for all personnel</li>
          <li><strong>Confidentiality Agreements:</strong> All employees and contractors sign confidentiality agreements</li>
          <li><strong>Limited Access:</strong> Access to personal data limited to employees who need it for their job functions</li>
          <li><strong>Incident Response Plan:</strong> Procedures for detecting, reporting, and responding to security incidents</li>
          <li><strong>Regular Audits:</strong> Periodic security assessments and compliance reviews</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3">8.3 Security Limitations</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Despite our security measures, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. While we strive to protect your personal information, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <strong>Your Responsibilities:</strong> You are responsible for maintaining the security of your Shopify account credentials. Never share your password with anyone, and notify us immediately if you suspect unauthorized access to your account.
        </p>

